  "configuration_id": "config_050",
  "reason": "Evidence: We have only one completed experiment (config_005: multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, weighted fusion → 53.2% acc / 51.6% F1). The most fundamental uncertainty is whether multimodal fusion actually adds value over a single modality, or whether the performance is driven primarily by one modality. Question: config_050 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is a clean ablation that removes the image modality while keeping the same RNA encoder and profile setting as config_005. This isolates the marginal contribution of the image branch. Why this is the best use of the next budget: If RNA-only with PCA performs comparably (~53%), we learn that the image modality is not adding value with this encoder and can redirect effort toward RNA encoder selection (scgpt, scvi) or profile settings. If it performs substantially worse, we confirm multimodal fusion is essential and should prioritize optimizing fusion strategy and image encoder. This single experiment partitions the remaining search space into very different strategic directions, making it the highest-information-gain choice under a limited budget."
}

